module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.stale_seed_hides_the_first_wins_conflict_population_the_fold_exposes

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

// THE POPULATION THE FOLD EXPOSES, RECORDED BY NAME (#14152 lane, manager ruling
// 2026-10-22: one row for the fold-census class; DFS done -- the class row
// gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.silent_first_wins_rebind_of_a_generic_type_variable_in_unify_generics
// owns the fail-open itself and deliberately quotes no counts; this row is its exposed-population
// sibling: what the repaired fold makes the REQUIRED path refuse, each site named by its
// enclosing declaration, with each class's repair owner and route. Charter 3 (vivid-carp-314)
// was told this row exists before filing theirs. No count or position is transcribed here:
// the three instruments named in the recipe are the sole authority for the population at any
// head, per DESIGN section 6 and section 3.)
data stale_seed_hides_the_first_wins_conflict_population_the_fold_exposes: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "stale_seed_hides_the_first_wins_conflict_population_the_fold_exposes" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
      ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "the capability of the required-path seed build to run green on a head whose stage0 seed realizes the unify_generics conflict check, with zero disagreement refusals emitted on all three gate closures -- reached when every named site below carries its repair (compiler-side or corpus-side) and the re-derivation recipe prints an empty population"
    }
  },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: the shipped stage0 seed was built while unify_generics was first-wins silent (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.silent_first_wins_rebind_of_a_generic_type_variable_in_unify_generics), so corpus call sites whose arguments disagree about one formal type variable compiled forever without a word, and the seed carried their mis-bound instances downstream. The seed is stale evidence of those calls' well-formedness: it proves only that the SILENT fold accepted them. When the fold reports conflicts, the hidden population becomes hard compile errors on the required path (the seed-build instrument refuses to emit), which is the correct direction -- an error stops masquerading as success -- but it also means a compiler-side repair lands RED over corpus defects the seed had been laundering, and RED with no named list is indistinguishable from a broken compiler.",

    "THE POPULATION, AS OBSERVED (first measured at head 0e6320f51286 + regen commit e9069e9bb7c7, the fold-realized vehicle head of PR #14711): the gate closures refuse a population of 'bound as' disagreement sites whose members are named below by ENCLOSING DECLARATION. This row transcribes no counts and no positions: the three instruments in the recipe are the authority for what the population is at any head, and each class receipt says how its members were disposed. Dispositions follow the manager's re-ruling (2026-10-22): the population shrinks by compiler-side fixes first; NOTHING here has a corpus owner routed yet.",

    "(A) OVER-REJECTIONS -- the fold refuses a pairing that is one type, and the refusal must be fixed COMPILER-SIDE before PR-2 lands; each class's RED is its named sites leaving ALL THREE gate populations, measured on PR-2's head: (A1) IDENTICAL-PRINT LEAF-VERSUS-LEAF, where the diagnostic shows the reader 'expected X, got X' -- members: the ShellSimpleCommand redirects field in dag/gunbc/remote_shell_command.dag (Primitive(PosixRedirection) versus itself), the integer_standard_integer_type_roster data row in src/v2/std/integer.dag (Primitive(StandardIntegerType) versus itself), and the two Optional-versus-its-own-printing sites, in the AuthoredUsesFunction type and the demand_census_alias_uniqueness function in src/v2/compiler/dependency_demand_census.dag. Owner: #14056 leaf-identity half -- leaf comparison by declaration identity, NEVER by printed text (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.node_type_shape_prints_applied_head_without_declaration_identity records why printed shape cannot carry this judgment). (A2) WRAPPER / UNRESOLVED-FORM ACTUALS, where the two sides differ only in the form the same inner declaration is carried in -- members: the type Int alias in src/v2/std/integer.dag (Primitive(Int) against a node spelled as that alias's application), the three Primitive-versus-Node(same carrier) sites in the type QualifiedName in src/v2/std/qualified_name.dag, the demand_engine_relate function in src/v2/std/demand_engine.dag and the list_snoc_item function in dag/std/algebra.dag, and the <kernel:String> kernel site (Primitive(List) bound against Primitive(String) -- see the text ruling inside (A4) before treating it as over-rejection). Owner: eager-cat-804's unify_child_actual in #14632 (type-argument children arrive as wrappers whose real type sits under inferred.Resolved) plus the representation PR, per manager routing; the bare-versus-applied pairing is decided by the fold's own generic_head_matches_application arm and needs render-level confirmation before it is called the same class. (A3) OWN-FORM LEAVES ESCAPING THE REPLACE ARM -- members: the map_insert function in dag/std/algebra.dag, where a call site hands the callee's own Map(K, V) formal straight to another generic call and K, V are the callee's own parameters (the dominant member by volume in the REQUIRED gate closure). Mechanism (measured on the PR-2 vehicle head; the guard named below exists ONLY on the unlanded PR-2 branch, as the planned repair, and is cited as a plan not as evidence): the fold's own-form recognition decides by scanning the bound node's params, but a call-site application node carries NO params, so a bound node whose leaves are the callee's own parameters is not recognized as unsettled and falls to the refusal instead of the REPLACE arm. This is PR-2's own fold bug and is fixed INSIDE PR-2, and measured (the fold-side class left the seed-build population with nothing joining; the repair keys on the leaf's declaration field being a DeclField TypeParameter -- the stamp resolve's binder_marked_type produces, not on spelling). HALF OF THIS CLASS IS NOT FOLD-SIDE: the name-keyed substitution at instantiate (the callee's formal parameter NAMES substituted into actual nodes) silently rewrites a real corpus type whose name shadows a formal, so the fold never sees the pairing; per the manager's ruling that substitution identity belongs to ONE authority -- the representation PR -- which lands BEFORE PR-2, and its acceptance test is the enrolled claim member corpus_type_shadow_named_like_formal_still_refuses in dag/test/claim/applied_constructor_type_equals.dag. (A4) ALIAS-VERSUS-OWN-RHS, where a v2.std.text alias reference meets its own unfolding -- members: the type String alias in src/v2/std/text.dag (its String spelling against its FreeMonoid<Char> right-hand side, both directions), appearing through the list_append function in dag/std/algebra.dag and through the map_insert region. DESIGN section 4's text ruling makes the v2.std.text alias String and its own RHS FreeMonoid<Char> ONE declaration (unlike the kernel-String crossing, which is a real wall -- gunbc.rung_drop.text_boundary_identity_wall); the fold peels childless aliases, and the applied-alias pairing needs the same single-declaration judgment through the alias body. Route: named by this row; the alias body is invisible to the compile fixture until the declaration-generation form arrives (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.container_alias_spellings_are_hand_written_from_a_runtime_roster names the capability).",

    "(B) FOLD-DEFECT SUSPECTS, NOT YET ROUTED TO ANY OWNER (manager re-ruling 2026-10-22: these move out of correct-closure on the mechanical print evidence and must be RE-MEASURED after the A1 leaf-identity fix and the A3 own-form guard land; route whatever survives). Members, named by enclosing declaration: the outcome_accepted function in src/v2/std/diagnostic.dag, which prints expected and got IDENTICALLY (the A1 identical-print class); the target_derive_supplemental_generic_bound_wire_requirement_apply function in src/v2/std/compilers/target_model.dag, which differs only by wrapper form on the same inner declaration (the A2 wrapper class); the bind_outcome and append_outcome_value functions in src/v2/std/diagnostic.dag and the python_g1_2_snoc_primitive_bundle function in src/v2/extdeps/languages/python.dag, whose bound side prints Product(Unit<>) -- the class row's kind (2) fabricated-placeholder caution (the placeholder arm belongs to gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.error_type_fabricated_as_a_type_by_total_accessors), so UNCONFIRMED until the bound side is shown to be a real Product(Unit<>) rather than a fabricated slot. A corpus owner who edits any of these call sites before re-measurement is repairing against a diagnostic the fold itself may be falsifying.",

    "(C) PARKED BEHIND AN OBSERVATION DEFECT, NOT ROUTED: the kernel-pseudo-file sites -- the <kernel:Int> site (a Product(Char<Primitive(Int)>) binding against a Primitive(Int) actual), the <kernel:String> and <kernel:Map> kernel sites named in (A2)/(A) -- print 'no position: no source index for this file', so a reader cannot locate the call site to repair it. The kernel pseudo-file carries no NewlineIndex; these sites wait on the diagnostic-position gap in the emitted-closure path, which is its own observation defect and NOT this row's class. gunbc.rung_drop.v1_required_lanes_withdrawn owns the required-path rung; this row does not claim it.",

    "RE-DERIVATION RECIPE (the only citation of these numbers is by this producer; anyone may re-run it): check out the head carrying the realized fold (stage0 v1_compiler_infer.rs contains the unify_generics conflict check), build release (cargo build --release --bin gunbc --bin claim_executor, -j6 or lower: the regen peaks at the 24 GiB cgroup cap), then run the three instruments that gate PR-2's landing and grep 'bound as' from each resolve failure: (1) the seed-build instrument -- ./target/release/gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/gunbc/instruments/seed_build_artifacts_regen.dag --function main_wet; (2) the witnesses workflow's //gunbc/instruments:self-host bazel target (the REQUIRED gate closure -- manager ruling 2026-10-22: its closure is the authority for can-PR-2-land; it carries sites the seed-build closure does not, and omits two it carries); (3) the heal workflow's heal_candidate_stage0 instrument (refuses on the same population). A fix is only done when its sites leave ALL THREE populations. No count or site list is transcribed in this row: a transcribed number rots unreachably, and the instruments' outputs are the authority. The population reaching zero with all three closures green is this row's trigger firing; at that point this row is deleted in the same change that lands the last site's repair.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "unify_generics", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
